        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "645fbcf7-885d-585f-b05a-d04f6c09362b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: James Gregory, Joseph McCarthy, Robert Stevens, Rory Calhoun, Mary Costa\n- Roles: Sen. John Iselin, General Ursus, Inspector Frank Luger\n- Works: The Manchurian Candidate, Beneath the Planet of the Apes, Barney Miller, The Big Caper\n- Topics: McCarthyism, Cold War fears of Communist subversion\n\nFacts:\n- Beginning in 1950, Joseph McCarthy became the most visible public face of a period in the United States when Cold War tensions fueled fears of widespread Communist subversion.\n- James Gregory was an American character actor born on December 23, 1911, and he was known for his deep, gravelly voice and brash roles.\n- The Big Caper is a 1957 crime drama film noir directed by Robert Stevens and starring Rory Calhoun, Mary Costa, and James Gregory.\n- James Gregory played the McCarthy-like Sen. John Iselin in The Manchurian Candidate in 1962.\n- James Gregory played General Ursus in Beneath the Planet of the Apes in 1970.\n- From 1975 to 1982, James Gregory played Inspector Frank Luger in the television sitcom Barney Miller.\n- James Gregory died on September 16, 2002.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
